  "narrative": "All estimates are signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive values support the registered claim. The new library-stratified estimates strongly confirm the accepted main effects. In the Avana library, MSI-high cells showed much stronger WRN dependency (+0.794, 95% CI +0.764 to +0.825, R41), essentially matching the accepted main and independently validated effect. In the KY library, SMARCA4-loss cells showed much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (+0.816, CI +0.777 to +0.856, R42), and KEAP1-loss cells showed the accepted less-negative/weaker NFE2L2 dependency (+0.794, CI +0.752 to +0.837, R44). These are very large on the dependency scale and make assay-artifact or single-library explanations implausible. Therefore H62, H63, and H65 are accepted and closed as stable stratum evidence. The KY USP7 estimate is directionally supportive but attenuated relative to the main effect: TP53-intact versus TP53-loss USP7 dependency was +0.212 (CI +0.051 to +0.373, R43), compared with roughly +0.40 in the overall and adenocarcinoma/batch strata. Because this is the only major accepted effect that appears technically context-dependent, I accept H64 as evidence of a positive association in KY while keeping it active and requesting independent validation; a null or reversed validation response would indicate library-specific attenuation without overturning the main USP7/TP53 claim. The new TMED10 results are essentially null: MYC amplification (+0.009, CI -0.014 to +0.031, R45), EGFR amplification (+0.004, CI -0.026 to +0.034, R46), and MSI-high (-0.016, CI -0.048 to +0.016, R47) do not support scientifically meaningful TMED10 dependency differences. The MSI-high null on TMED10 is useful as a specificity check: MSI-high has a very large accepted association with WRN but not with TMED10, supporting WRN-specific biology rather than a broad screen-quality or MSI confound. H66-H68 are rejected and closed. The formal lineage-subtype and TP53-status interactions for the four accepted main effects are all small and statistically null: H15 SMARCA2 (-0.028, CI -0.076 to +0.020, R48), H19 WRN (-0.021, CI -0.085 to +0.042, R49), H52 USP7 (-0.038, CI -0.190 to +0.115, R50), H53 NFE2L2 (-0.012, CI -0.057 to +0.033, R51), and H21 NFE2L2 by TP53 status (-0.018, CI -0.069 to +0.034, R52). These do not support meaningful modification of the accepted associations. H52 has the widest interval, but even its extreme lower bound would not erase the USP7/TP53-intact association, and the point estimate is small; I therefore reject it as a meaningful adenocarcinoma modifier and close it. The next priority is to broaden coverage and test remaining mechanistic leads, especially KRAS/STK11/BRAF-related dependencies, USP7/KRAS modifiers, ARID1A/SMARCA2 relationships, and transcription/replication-related hypotheses such as MYC-POLR2A, MYC-KIF18A, and BRCA2-DHX9.",
  "research_notes": "Updated main conclusions in this dataset: MSI-high is robustly associated with much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss is robustly associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; TP53 intact is robustly associated with stronger USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss is robustly associated with less-negative NFE2L2 dependency. All four main effects have independent validation and are stable in major tested strata. New direct stratum checks: Avana/MSI-high/WRN H62 accepted +0.794; KY/SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 H63 accepted +0.816; KY/KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 H65 accepted +0.794; KY/TP53-intact/USP7 H64 accepted but attenuated +0.212 and validation requested. Formal lineage and TP53-status interactions for these main effects are null and closed. TMED10 is not associated with MYC amplification, EGFR amplification, or MSI-high in a meaningful way; MSI-high/TMED10 null supports WRN specificity. Next analyses should use unrun active registered claims: KRAS-related tests H1/H25/H44/H57/H58, BRAF tests H3/H26, USP7/KRAS modifiers H16/H40/H41, ARID1A/SMARCA2 H37/H38/H61, MYC/replication-transcription H30/H56, BRCA2/DHX9 H32, EGFR-dependency refinements H5/H14/H59, and any useful negative controls such as H17/H24. Avoid more validation unless a new robust unvalidated association emerges or H64 validation changes the interpretation of USP7/TP53 context dependence.",
