  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the registered claim. H9 tests whether SMARCA4-loss cells have stronger dependency_SMARCA2 than SMARCA4-intact cells. Its original discovery estimate was +0.784 (95% CI +0.765 to +0.803, R9), and the independent validation response gives +0.807 (independent CI +0.777 to +0.838, R26). Both intervals exclude zero by very large margins, the effects are more than two dependency-score standard deviations, and the discovery and validation point estimates are nearly identical. H9 is therefore accepted with independent support. I keep the investigation active because biologically relevant ARID1A-context modifiers of SMARCA2 remain unresolved, but the main SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association is now one of the most robust findings in this dataset. H64 tests the same TP53-intact versus TP53-loss USP7 association within the KY CRISPR library. The discovery direct estimate was positive but attenuated relative to the overall effect: +0.212 (95% CI +0.051 to +0.373, R43). The new independent validation gives +0.336 with an independent CI +0.129 to +0.544, which also excludes zero at the multiplicity-adjusted validation level. Therefore the KY-specific USP7 effect is not a null technical artifact; TP53-intact cells still show stronger USP7 dependency in KY. However, the point estimate is lower than the overall validation effect of about +0.435, so this finding supports context-dependent attenuation rather than absence. H64 is accepted and closed as validated direct stratum evidence. Overall, the dataset-supported robust associations are now: MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; TP53-intact cells are associated with stronger USP7 dependency; and KEAP1-loss cells have less-negative/weaker NFE2L2 dependency relative to KEAP1-intact cells, which is the reverse of the original mechanistic guess and should be described as a measured association rather than causal confirmation. These main effects are supported by independent validation and are stable across major tested strata, including adenocarcinoma, batch_a, Avana for WRN, KY for SMARCA2 and NFE2L2, and KY for USP7. Formal interactions for lineage subtype and TP53 status were small and null. Negative controls and TMED10 specificity probes are null, arguing against a simple assay artifact or broad MSI confound. Remaining uncertainty is concentrated in smaller or imprecise comparisons: KRAS-mutation effects on KRAS, BRAF, STAT3, and USP7; EGFR-amplification effects on EGFR dependency; ARID1A-context modifiers of SMARCA2; MYC amplification effects on POLR2A/KIF18A; and BRCA2-loss effects on DHX9. No further validation is needed for the four main effects or for H64; validation should be reserved if a new large, unvalidated robust association emerges. The next analyses should run the active registered KRAS/BRAF/STK11, ARID1A/SMARCA2, USP7/KRAS modifier, MYC/transcription-replication, BRCA2/DHX9, and EGFR-dependency comparisons to map the boundary of the robust findings rather than retesting the main effects.",
  "research_notes": "Main accepted dataset associations: H8 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H9 SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H12 TP53-intact -> stronger USP7 dependency; H13 KEAP1-loss -> less-negative NFE2L2 dependency. H7 original KEAP1 direction is rejected/closed; H13 is accepted reversed claim. All four main effects have independent validation and are stable across tested strata. H64 KY TP53-intact/USP7 is accepted and closed: KY direct discovery +0.212, independent validation +0.336; positive but attenuated, not absent. H9 validated with R26 +0.807; keep active only for ARID1A modifier follow-up. Context/null checks: H62 Avana WRN +0.794 accepted/closed; H63 KY SMARCA2 +0.816 accepted/closed; H65 KY NFE2L2 +0.794 accepted/closed; lineage interactions H15/H19/H52/H53 and TP53 interaction H21 null/closed; TMED10 MYC/EGFR/MSI null/closed; marker controls null. Next priorities: run active unregistered? active registered claims: ARID1A/SMARCA2 H37/H38/H61, USP7/KRAS H16/H40/H41, KRAS/STK11/BRAF H25/H26/H44/H57/H58, MYC-POLR2A/KIF18A H30/H56, BRCA2-DHX9 H32, EGFR refinements H5/H14/H59, negative controls H17/H24. Reserve validation for new robust unvalidated effects. Interpret all conclusions as dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}
